The Safe Voice application was developed using Android Studio as the main development environment. Android Studio provides the necessary tools for building, testing, and debugging Android applications. The backend of the app was developed using Java, which handles the core functionality and logic of the system, while the frontend was designed using XML for creating the user interface. Android Studio also includes an emulator and built-in debugging tools that helped in ensuring the performance and functionality of the application during development. This platform made it possible to efficiently create a reliable and user-friendly reporting application.
